00:31:40,650 --> 00:31:40,850
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, yeah.

481
00:31:41,030 --> 00:31:43,471
[SPEAKER_02]: Did that make a better mix on the saliva?

482
00:31:43,491 --> 00:31:43,911
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

483
00:31:45,971 --> 00:31:48,212
[SPEAKER_02]: Did it get it nice and brown and dirty?

484
00:31:48,492 --> 00:31:50,833
[SPEAKER_02]: I chewed tobacco on one side and gum on the other.

485
00:31:52,714 --> 00:31:53,935
[SPEAKER_02]: You'd get it mixed up, I hope.

486
00:31:56,637 --> 00:32:03,522
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, did you ever slip?

487
00:32:03,542 --> 00:32:04,482
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, once in a while.

488
00:32:05,063 --> 00:32:06,223
[SPEAKER_00]: Not very often, though.

489
00:32:08,005 --> 00:32:10,106
[SPEAKER_00]: Did the catchers have much trouble with that spitball?

490
00:32:10,927 --> 00:32:11,487
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, no.

491
00:32:12,168 --> 00:32:13,569
[SPEAKER_00]: I had a good catcher shock.

492
00:32:14,069 --> 00:32:17,351
