525
00:33:50,704 --> 00:33:51,184
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, yeah.

526
00:33:52,252 --> 00:33:55,233
[SPEAKER_00]: I think 10,000 is the highest I ever got there.

527
00:33:57,074 --> 00:33:58,774
[SPEAKER_02]: What year would that have been?

528
00:33:59,154 --> 00:33:59,354
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh.

529
00:33:59,974 --> 00:34:04,176
[SPEAKER_02]: About 1920 or 21?

530
00:34:04,376 --> 00:34:07,157
[SPEAKER_00]: I think I had a pretty good year in 17.

531
00:34:07,297 --> 00:34:07,617
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

532
00:34:07,857 --> 00:34:11,558
[SPEAKER_00]: I think one of my parents did.

533
00:34:12,938 --> 00:34:13,539
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

534
00:34:13,619 --> 00:34:19,140
[SPEAKER_00]: In 18, I pitched about four or five games and then I had to go to whatchacallit.

535
00:34:19,320 --> 00:34:19,600
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

536
00:34:24,781 --> 00:34:26,061
