[SPEAKER_02]: I see Peckinpah in Cleveland.

1421
01:27:29,583 --> 01:27:30,884
[SPEAKER_02]: I've talked to him a couple of times.

1422
01:27:30,924 --> 01:27:35,667
[SPEAKER_02]: He's doing very well, although he's slowing up a little bit.

1423
01:27:35,687 --> 01:27:38,670
[SPEAKER_02]: He goes to Florida still, I think, with his brother.

1424
01:27:39,710 --> 01:27:52,440
[SPEAKER_03]: Well, we were invited to Bradenton the end of this month, and then also Governor Askew has the banquet.

1425
01:27:52,540 --> 01:27:54,001
[SPEAKER_03]: I think it's their 30th?

1426
01:27:55,767 --> 01:27:57,528
[SPEAKER_02]: They have a hall of fame, don't they, down there?

1427
01:27:57,848 --> 01:28:02,170
[SPEAKER_03]: I don't know, but it's their 30th baseball banquet.

1428
01:28:02,750 --> 01:28:06,812
[SPEAKER_03]: I presume the Chamber of Commerce, that's where the letter comes from.

1429
01:28:06,832 --> 01:28:14,335
[SPEAKER_03]: But of course, I was invited this year, too, which I've never been before.

1430
01:28:14,455 --> 01:28:18,376
[SPEAKER_03]: But now, he couldn't even travel with me.

1431
01:28:18,396 --> 01:28:25,239
[SPEAKER_03]: Because the barber comes here, and he hasn't been out of the house for five years.

1432
01:28:26,364 --> 01:28:27,765
[SPEAKER_02]: That's a lovely house.

1433
01:28:28,245 --> 01:28:29,606
[SPEAKER_03]: Yes, it is.

1434
01:28:29,667 --> 01:28:38,533
[SPEAKER_03]: Maybe it doesn't seem that long to you, but... Well, as long as you can see the ball games there, that's a big help.

1435
01:28:39,274 --> 01:28:42,096
[SPEAKER_02]: There are some games played today, I think.

1436
01:28:42,856 --> 01:28:43,137
[SPEAKER_03]: No.

1437
01:28:44,738 --> 01:28:51,483
[SPEAKER_03]: No, what you probably read was that they were going to start spring training.

1438
01:28:51,761 --> 01:28:54,562
[SPEAKER_02]: They are, definitely.

1439
01:28:54,582 --> 01:28:58,803
[SPEAKER_02]: Commissioner, I guess, there's a rumor he's going to open the camps by himself, by his own authority.

1440
01:29:00,183 --> 01:29:02,684
[SPEAKER_03]: I didn't get a chance to read the paper today.

1441
01:29:02,964 --> 01:29:06,644
[SPEAKER_02]: If they don't open today or tomorrow, they can't open the season, they figure.

1442
01:29:06,664 --> 01:29:10,725
[SPEAKER_03]: Well, they figured they have to have three weeks.

1443
01:29:11,566 --> 01:29:15,487
[SPEAKER_03]: So I think he said that it was going to start on time.

1444
01:29:15,687 --> 01:29:17,647
[SPEAKER_03]: Was it the 8th, his opening day?

1445
01:29:17,687 --> 01:29:17,947
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

1446
01:29:17,987 --> 01:29:20,328
[SPEAKER_03]: In Cincinnati.

1447
01:29:22,724 --> 01:29:28,909
[SPEAKER_02]: I think we watch all the ballgames that are on here.

1448
01:29:29,990 --> 01:29:31,992
[SPEAKER_02]: Do the Cubs televise all their games?

1449
01:29:32,352 --> 01:29:32,613
[SPEAKER_02]: Huh?

1450
01:29:32,753 --> 01:29:34,474
[SPEAKER_02]: Do the Cubs televise all their games?

1451
01:29:35,135 --> 01:29:35,515
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

1452
01:29:35,695 --> 01:29:39,559
[SPEAKER_02]: You got baseball every day then almost, huh?

1453
01:29:39,639 --> 01:29:39,899
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

1454
01:29:40,239 --> 01:29:48,726
[SPEAKER_03]: Now the thing is, now so many of the Sox games are at night, and by that time, Babe is in bed and asleep when they start.

1455
01:29:49,973 --> 01:29:52,714
[SPEAKER_02]: Of course, the Cub games are all daytime when they're home.

1456
01:29:53,134 --> 01:29:58,535
[SPEAKER_03]: But then, you see, he doesn't get to see the Sox all the time because they're at night.

1457
01:29:58,635 --> 01:29:59,335
[SPEAKER_03]: Except on weekends.

1458
01:29:59,435 --> 01:30:05,757
[SPEAKER_03]: Oh, they have a few day games.

1459
01:30:07,797 --> 01:30:11,878
[SPEAKER_02]: There's a great old ballpark down there.

1460
01:30:13,218 --> 01:30:15,099
[SPEAKER_02]: One of the few of the old ones that are left.

1461
01:30:15,619 --> 01:30:17,259
[SPEAKER_00]: I was actually wondering what they're doing.

1462
01:30:17,779 --> 01:30:19,780
[SPEAKER_00]: They're going to take a lot of things out

1463
01:30:22,425 --> 01:30:24,326
[SPEAKER_03]: Oh, they took up the turf.

1464
01:30:24,386 --> 01:30:27,328
[SPEAKER_03]: I wish I had gotten down there, because... You know why?

1465
01:30:27,789 --> 01:30:36,134
[SPEAKER_03]: They're taking up the artificial turf or whatever you call it, and anybody could come in and take a piece of it.

1466
01:30:36,974 --> 01:30:47,521
[SPEAKER_03]: And I would have liked to have gone down, because then when you practice golf, you know, in the backyard, you could hit on that instead of tearing up all the sod.

1467
01:30:48,861 --> 01:30:49,722
[SPEAKER_02]: You play golf there?

1468
01:30:51,860 --> 01:31:01,891
[SPEAKER_03]: Well, I took lessons in February, and I've been playing off and on for 52 years, but I never knew how to hold a club.

